  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Lifesaving Reproductive Health Services for IDPs affected by escalating Crisis in Ma&#x2019;rib</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main engagements under the project include:procuring and distribution of a whole range of RH kits, commodities, equipment, and supplies for the delivery of RH services at the health facilities, incentive payment to medical doctors, midwives, and nurses to ensure the provision of 24/7 motherhood services within the BEmONC and CEmONC Health Facilities and supporting 2 outreach mobile teams and community midwifery in Marib. The project targets 120,000 affected people with its Health-SRH engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
